# Commit Message Rules

## Format
All commit messages must follow the Conventional Commit standard:

<type>[scope]: <description>

## Allowed Types
- `feat` - A new feature
- `fix` - A bug fix
- `refactor` - A code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
- `perf` - A code change that improves performance
- `docs` - Documentation only changes
- `test` - Adding missing tests or correcting existing tests
- `chore` - Changes to the build process or auxiliary tools

## Required Scopes
The following scopes are required for changes to specific areas:
- `agents` - Changes related to agent functionality
- `core` - Changes related to core system functionality
- `config` - Changes related to configuration

## Subject Line
- Maximum 50 characters
- Must be lowercase
- No trailing period

## Body
- Each line must be wrapped at 72 characters
- Explain what and why, not how

## Footer
- Must include an issue reference in the format: `Closes #123`
- The footer is mandatory

## Automation
Always use `scripts/generate_commit.py` when staging changes to ensure commit messages follow these standards.